CM_ BO_ 53 "VCU status message (subset). Message ID / DLC / signal bit-layout copied as-is from the real vehicle network database (20250519_STD_DB_CAR_R2.0_2024_Local_FD-SBCM_DRV_SBCM_DRV_FD_v25.05.01.dbc) for ES95486-02 VCU-condition-gating study. Only VCU_EvDrvRdySta is modeled here; the other real signals carried by this message are intentionally omitted as out of scope for this project.";
CM_ SG_ 53 VCU_EvDrvRdySta "VCU_EvDriveReadyStatus. ES95486-02 Table 3.1.1.1 (EV row) example signal; used as the project's 'VCU condition', which replaces the spec's generic 'Engine condition' for this EV project. Real-network GenMsgCycleTime=50ms, GenSigTimeoutTime=500ms (see VehicleCondition.cin).";
CM_ BO_ 977 "BCM status message (subset). Message ID / DLC / signal bit-layout copied as-is from the real vehicle network database (20250519_STD_DB_CAR_R2.0_2024_Local_FD-SBCM_DRV_SBCM_DRV_FD_v25.05.01.dbc) for ES95486-02 IGN-condition-gating study. Only BCM_Ign1InSta is modeled here (project decision: IGN1 only, BCM_Ign2InSta intentionally not modeled); the other real signals carried by this message are intentionally omitted as out of scope for this project.";
CM_ SG_ 977 BCM_Ign1InSta "BCM_Ignition1InputStatus. Used as the project's 'IGN condition'. ES95486-02 does not define IGN signal semantics itself (only the combined phrase 'Engine stop, IGN on'); this signal/value mapping is copied from the real network database. Real-network GenMsgCycleTime=200ms, GenSigTimeoutTime=1500ms (see VehicleCondition.cin).";

